# Rank 1587 / CVE-2026-32096: Plunk's SNS webhook fetched the
# SubscribeURL straight from the request body, so any poster chose
# the URL the server fetched -- internal addresses included
# (server-side request forgery, CWE-918). handleWebhook in
# apps/api/src/controllers/Webhooks.ts did `const confirmResponse =
# await fetch(req.body.SubscribeURL);` on a SubscriptionConfirmation
# -- the SNS contract says that URL belongs to Amazon, but nothing
# checked. Pool commit b8f1ad9ab5 is the real fix (COMMIT_OK --
# "fix: Verify SNS URL before sending fetch request"): the value is
# type-checked, parsed with new URL, and the protocol must be https
# with the hostname matching /^sns\.[a-z0-9-]+\.amazonaws\.com$/ --
# otherwise 400 -- before the fetch. No pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, rule reports, guard uncredited. VYQL-RF-001 reports the
# vulnerable path on the real code: at the fix parent, source
# code.HttpInput at Webhooks.ts:41 -> sink code.UrlFetch at :41 (the
# bare fetch of req.body.SubscribeURL), `unless
# core.AllowlistValidation` unsatisfied. The finding does not clear
# at the fix: the guard is an inline regex test (SNS_HOST_RE.test on
# the parsed hostname) plus a protocol comparison, and no binding
# credits an arbitrary local regex/protocol pair as
# AllowlistValidation -- control-at-a-distance, the same shape as
# ranks 1542 (helper-returned hardening) and 1555 (regex-allowlist
# guards). A binding on Plunk's own SNS_HOST_RE would detect this
# application rather than the weakness; the generic piece is
# inline-predicate guards as credited controls. Measured on the real
# code: one RF-001 at both revisions (the fix's finding sits at :65,
# the fetch inside the validated branch); an unrelated INJ-072
# heuristic row appears at :32 at both revisions. No new
# ENGINE-GAPS.md row (the helper-boundary row at 1542 states the
# gap). No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1587 records the
# bare request-URL fetch and the validated form, both expecting
# VYQL-RF-001: the rule fires today on both; when guard-credit
# vocabulary lands, the validated form must flip to reject.

test "rank1587: the webhook fetches the url it is posted"
  lang javascript
  file apps/api/src/controllers/Webhooks.ts
  expect VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  export async function handleWebhook(req, res) {
      if (req.body.Type === 'SubscriptionConfirmation') {
          signale.info('Subscribe URL:', req.body.SubscribeURL);

          const confirmResponse = await fetch(req.body.SubscribeURL);
          if (!confirmResponse.ok) {
              throw new Error('Failed to confirm SNS subscription');
          }
      }
      return res.status(200).json({ success: true });
  }
  ```

test "rank1587: the fix validates the sns host before fetching"
  lang javascript
  file apps/api/src/controllers/Webhooks.ts
  expect VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  export async function handleWebhook(req, res) {
      if (req.body.Type === 'SubscriptionConfirmation') {
          const subscribeURL = req.body.SubscribeURL;
          if (typeof subscribeURL !== 'string') {
              return res.status(400).json({ success: false, message: 'Invalid SubscribeURL' });
          }

          let parsedURL;
          try {
              parsedURL = new URL(subscribeURL);
          } catch {
              return res.status(400).json({ success: false, message: 'Invalid SubscribeURL' });
          }

          const SNS_HOST_RE = /^sns\.[a-z0-9-]+\.amazonaws\.com$/;
          if (parsedURL.protocol !== 'https:' || !SNS_HOST_RE.test(parsedURL.hostname)) {
              signale.warn('SNS SubscriptionConfirmation rejected');
              return res.status(400).json({ success: false, message: 'Invalid SubscribeURL' });
          }

          const confirmResponse = await fetch(parsedURL.toString());
          if (!confirmResponse.ok) {
              throw new Error('Failed to confirm SNS subscription');
          }
      }
      return res.status(200).json({ success: true });
  }
  ```
